# Cloudflare Pages: NO SPA catch-all here (see P0-1 spec, fast-program/I-platform).
# Pages serves a prerendered file whenever one matches the path, and falls
# back to the root shell for other paths (native SPA behaviour, active
# because there is no top-level 404.html). A `/* /index.html 200` rule
# would shadow EVERY prerendered page — Cloudflare follows redirect rules
# even when a static asset matches the request
# (developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/: "Redirects
# are always followed, regardless of whether or not an asset matches the
# incoming request"). Do not re-add it.
# Genuine URL moves go here as explicit static rules, e.g.:
# /old-path /new-path 301
# NOTE (28 Nov 2026, verified live): the catch-all Pages Function
# (functions/[[path]].js) intercepts every request BEFORE _redirects
# rules are evaluated, so rules added here do NOT fire — URL moves
# must be implemented in the Function's onRequest instead. The
# duplicate-tool redirects (pdf-page-extractor -> pdf-splitter,
# jpg-to-pdf -> image-to-pdf) live there.
